155:{character:Yumeko Jabami}Calm down, Mary.
157:Mary ignores Yumeko's calls and leaves on her own. In a matter of seconds, she is out of sight.
158:{character:Yumeko Jabami}Mary probably has her own plans. Don't worry, she can take care of herself.
159:Saotome, who has lost count of how many times she has returned to the shrine gate, is resting against the torii pillar.
160:{character:Kirari Momobami}Good evening, Mary Saotome. Are you also here to visit?
283:{character:Wanjirou}Ron!
285:{character:Wanjirou}I told you I'm not a dog monster! I'm the Dog God, woof!
286:{character:Wanjirou}Nonsense, woof! We are an authentic shrine, and I am an authentic god.
287:{character:Wanjirou}How dare you mortals be so rude... Never mind. I'm not some inferior god who bickers with mortals. Tell me, what are your wishes, woof?
288:{character:Mary Saotome}Screw it. There's a path there. If you don't show me the way, I'll find my own way.
289:{character:Yumeko Jabami}Wait, Mary, Mary—
290:{character:Midari Ikishima}Wait, that 'blonde loser-cat' is here, too?
291:{character:Miki Nikaidou}So, shall we place some bets? Like... Do you want to play a penalty game?
292:{character:Wanjirou}Woof?! What? Are you thinking what I'm thinking?!
293:{character:Miki&Yumeko}Oops.//nOops.
295:{character:Miki Nikaidou}Of course! Ichihime has confirmed it's spicy and delicious.
296:Hyakkaou Private Academy sees field trips as an important part of education, so, naturally they have given the students a "research topic" to finish.
297:And of course, this topic is really Hyakkaou-styled.
327:{character:Miki Nikaidou}Welcome to the Mahjong Soul Shrine, our two lost guests.
328:{character:Miki Nikaidou}Oops, my bad. Then, please let the shrine staff member meticulously comfort our nervous guests!
329:{character:Miki Nikaidou}To leave, you need some help from 'fate', hehe.
